Q: Property &#39;example&#39; does not exist on type &#39; componentName&#39; A: <p>Several problem:</p>
<p>in interface you have</p>
<pre><code>export interface DataLayer {
    name: {};
    ...
}

</code></pre>
<p>This indicate that name is an Object (well really an Object with no property)</p>
<p>Do you want to say?</p>
<pre><code>export interface DataLayer {
    name: string; //&lt;--if is a string
    ...
}

</code></pre>
<p>In <code>homeComponent</code> you have</p>
<pre><code>dataLayer: DataLayer = {
    name: {{this.results[1][0].name}}
    ...
}
</code></pre>
<p>the use of <code>{{``}}</code> to interpolate is ONLY in template, in code is simply</p>
<pre><code>dataLayer: DataLayer = {
    name: this.results[1][0].name
    ...
}
</code></pre>
<p>The error <code>&quot;Property 'results' does not exist on type 'HomeComponent'.&quot;</code> it's because you are not defined a property 'result' in component.</p>
<p>In HomeComponent define</p>
<pre><code>result:any=null
//or 
result:DataLayer={}

</code></pre>
